From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weegee <748975+Weegee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:52:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drv: queue work on system_dfl_wq instead of the deprecated
 system_wq

Linux 7.2 marks system_wq (and system_unbound_wq) deprecated and logs
"enqueued on deprecated workqueue" once per work function; on the test
machine this appears for fthd_idle_work on every boot.

The idle power-off, the frame watchdog and the recovery need no CPU
locality and sleep for long (power cycle, firmware boot), so they go
to the unbound system_dfl_wq. recover_work moves from schedule_work()
to queue_work(system_dfl_wq, ...).

irq_work stays on schedule_work(): that is system_percpu_wq since
6.17, not deprecated, and keeps the bottom half on the interrupted
CPU.

system_dfl_wq exists since 6.17. Older kernels get system_unbound_wq,
which is the same unbound queue under its old name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fthd_drv.c  | 4 ++--
 fthd_drv.h  | 5 +++++
 fthd_v4l2.c | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fthd_drv.c b/fthd_drv.c
index 83e0ee8..41e0e70 100644
--- a/fthd_drv.c
+++ b/fthd_drv.c
@@ -640,7 +640,7 @@ out:
 
 void fthd_schedule_recovery(struct fthd_private *dev_priv)
 {
-	schedule_work(&dev_priv->recover_work);
+	queue_work(system_dfl_wq, &dev_priv->recover_work);
 }
 
 static void fthd_idle_work(struct work_struct *work)
@@ -662,7 +662,7 @@ void fthd_schedule_idle(struct fthd_private *dev_priv)
 
 	if (ms >= 0 && !dev_priv->streaming && !dev_priv->powered_off &&
 	    !dev_priv->suspended && !dev_priv->removing)
-		mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &dev_priv->idle_work,
+		mod_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &dev_priv->idle_work,
 				 msecs_to_jiffies(ms));
 }
 
diff --git a/fthd_drv.h b/fthd_drv.h
index 7c040b4..2a6af53 100644
--- a/fthd_drv.h
+++ b/fthd_drv.h
@@ -25,6 +25,11 @@
 #include "fthd_buffer.h"
 #include "fthd_v4l2.h"
 
+/* system_dfl_wq was added in 6.17; before that it was system_unbound_wq */
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 17, 0)
+#define system_dfl_wq system_unbound_wq
+#endif
+
 #define FTHD_PCI_S2_IO  0
 #define FTHD_PCI_S2_MEM 2
 #define FTHD_PCI_ISP_IO 4
diff --git a/fthd_v4l2.c b/fthd_v4l2.c
index 985905b..220d840 100644
--- a/fthd_v4l2.c
+++ b/fthd_v4l2.c
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@ static int fthd_buffer_queue_setup(
  */
 void fthd_frame_watchdog_kick(struct fthd_private *dev_priv)
 {
-	mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &dev_priv->frame_watchdog,
+	mod_delayed_work(system_dfl_wq, &dev_priv->frame_watchdog,
 			 msecs_to_jiffies(FTHD_FRAME_TIMEOUT_MS));
 }
 
